# Audio channels and mixing
@scenario tutorial_lesson_36
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/36_audio_channels.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt cue]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: This exercise separates a one-shot sound from the title music. Open it from the title screen so you can hear both channels.
@label compare
> Play a one-shot cue -> sound
> Pause the music -> pause_music
> Resume the music -> resume_music
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
@label sound
# region cue
[sfx assets/tutorial/welcome.wav]
# endregion
ginger: The cue uses the sound effects channel. Replay with effects at zero and music left audible.
[jump compare]
@label pause_music
[bgm_pause]
ginger: The music is paused. You can still play the cue.
[jump compare]
@label resume_music
[bgm_resume]
ginger: The music resumes at its previous position.
[jump compare]
@label return_hub
[bgm_resume]
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_36]
[flag tutorial_done_36]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_7]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Music is paused and the cue remains audible. What does this show?
> The pause command failed. -> practice_hint
> The effects channel can play independently. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: BGM pause affects the music track. Restore it before leaving the lab.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: BGM pause affects the music track. Restore it before leaving the lab.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the interactive lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Which channel does the one-shot sfx command use?
> Sound effects. -> correct
> Background music. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: The cue and the BGM have separate controls.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: The cue and the BGM have separate controls.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
